    {
      "type": "note",
      "content": "Number + counter combinations trigger phonetic changes. 一本 (ippon), 三本 (sanbon), 六本 (roppon) : the pattern follows Japanese sound rules. Don't try to memorise all variants at once. Learn the counter first and pick up the sound changes through exposure."
